    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d837">

                <pb facs="0714" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/2512</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Ellis O. Briggs of the Division of
                        the American Republics</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-29">May 29, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Cotton gave me the following information concerning Mr. Traphagen’s meeting
                    with Ambassador Turbay on May 28:</p>
                <p>The Ambassador indicated that notwithstanding the unsatisfactory Colombian
                    economic situation, he personally favored a permanent settlement at this time of
                    the Federal debt. He offered 3% service and funding of 50% of the arrears.</p>
                <p>Mr. Traphagen asked if the Ambassador would consider 3% and funding of all of the
                    arrears.</p>
                <p>Ambassador Turbay took this under advisement and it was left that he would get in
                    touch with Mr. Traphagen shortly. Mr. Traphagen is reportedly “hopeful.”</p>
                <p>Mr. Joe Cotton said he expected to see Mr. Laylin<anchor n="8" xml:id="d837-f1"/>
                    on May 31.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ellis O. Briggs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d837-f1" n="8" xml:id="d837-f1-content">
                <p>John Laylin, of Covington, Burling, Rublee, Acheson &amp; Shorb, counsel for the
                    Colombian Ambassador.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
